{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"g_root","type":"group","label":"Root & Interfaces","x":-60,"y":-60,"width":640,"height":840},
		{"id":"g_list","type":"group","label":"List (ordered, duplicates)","x":640,"y":-60,"width":760,"height":440},
		{"id":"g_set","type":"group","label":"Set (unique)","x":640,"y":420,"width":760,"height":460},
		{"id":"g_complex","type":"group","label":"Complexity Reference","x":640,"y":920,"width":760,"height":300},
		{"id":"g_queue","type":"group","label":"Queue / Deque","x":1460,"y":-60,"width":720,"height":440},
		{"id":"g_map","type":"group","label":"Map (key to value)","x":1460,"y":420,"width":820,"height":800},
		{"id":"g_key","type":"group","label":"Key Concepts","x":-60,"y":820,"width":640,"height":620},
		{"id":"g_conc","type":"group","label":"Concurrency","x":2340,"y":420,"width":660,"height":720},
		{"id":"index","type":"file","file":"03 Java/05 Collections Framework/00 Collections Framework Index.md","x":-20,"y":0,"width":260,"height":55,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"hub","type":"file","file":"03 Java/05 Collections Framework/01 Collections Framework.md","x":-20,"y":75,"width":260,"height":55,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"iface","type":"text","x":-20,"y":155,"width":560,"height":250,"text":"## Interface Hierarchy\n`Iterable`\n└ `Collection`\n  ├ `List` — ordered, allows duplicates\n  ├ `Set` — no duplicates\n  └ `Queue` / `Deque`\n\n`Map<K,V>` — **separate** hierarchy (key → value)\n\n> Program to interfaces; pick impl by access pattern."},
		{"id":"utility","type":"text","x":-20,"y":425,"width":560,"height":150,"text":"## `Collections` & `Arrays` utilities\n- `Collections.sort / binarySearch / reverse / shuffle`\n- `Collections.unmodifiableList`, `synchronizedMap`, `emptyList`\n- `Arrays.asList` (fixed-size view), `Arrays.sort`"},
		{"id":"immutable","type":"text","x":-20,"y":595,"width":560,"height":150,"text":"## Immutable collections\n- `List.of` / `Set.of` / `Map.of` — reject nulls, fixed-size\n- `List.copyOf`, unmodifiable views\n- Prefer immutable + defensive copies; safe as map keys"},
		{"id":"list","type":"file","file":"03 Java/05 Collections Framework/03 List.md","x":680,"y":10,"width":250,"height":55,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"arraylist","type":"file","file":"03 Java/05 Collections Framework/04 ArrayList.md","x":680,"y":90,"width":250,"height":55},
		{"id":"linkedlist","type":"file","file":"03 Java/05 Collections Framework/05 LinkedList.md","x":680,"y":165,"width":250,"height":55},
		{"id":"vector","type":"file","file":"03 Java/05 Collections Framework/06 Vector.md","x":680,"y":240,"width":250,"height":55},
		{"id":"listc","type":"text","x":960,"y":90,"width":400,"height":240,"text":"## List internals\n- **ArrayList**: backing array, grow ~1.5×, O(1) get, O(n) mid-insert, cache-friendly → **default**\n- **LinkedList**: doubly-linked, O(1) ends, O(n) index, also a `Deque`\n- **Vector**: legacy, every method `synchronized` → avoid"},
		{"id":"set","type":"file","file":"03 Java/05 Collections Framework/07 Set.md","x":680,"y":470,"width":250,"height":55,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"hashset","type":"file","file":"03 Java/05 Collections Framework/08 HashSet.md","x":680,"y":550,"width":250,"height":55},
		{"id":"linkedhashset","type":"file","file":"03 Java/05 Collections Framework/09 LinkedHashSet.md","x":680,"y":625,"width":250,"height":55},
		{"id":"treeset","type":"file","file":"03 Java/05 Collections Framework/10 TreeSet.md","x":680,"y":700,"width":250,"height":55},
		{"id":"setc","type":"text","x":960,"y":545,"width":400,"height":250,"text":"## Set internals\n- Uniqueness via `equals()` + `hashCode()`\n- **HashSet** → backed by HashMap, O(1), no order\n- **LinkedHashSet** → insertion order\n- **TreeSet** → backed by TreeMap (red-black), sorted, O(log n), `NavigableSet`"},
		{"id":"complexity","type":"text","x":680,"y":970,"width":680,"height":230,"text":"## Complexity (average)\n| Op | ArrayList | LinkedList | Hash* | Tree* |\n|----|-----------|------------|-------|-------|\n| get/contains | O(1)/O(n) | O(n) | O(1) | O(log n) |\n| add (end) | ~O(1) | O(1) | O(1) | O(log n) |\n| remove (mid) | O(n) | O(1)* | O(1) | O(log n) |\n\n*LinkedList O(1) only with a node reference. HashMap worst case O(log n) after treeify."},
		{"id":"queue","type":"file","file":"03 Java/05 Collections Framework/11 Queue.md","x":1500,"y":10,"width":250,"height":55,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"qc1","type":"text","x":1500,"y":90,"width":640,"height":120,"text":"## Deque / Queue\n- `ArrayDeque` = fast stack **and** queue (prefer over `Stack`/`LinkedList`)\n- Exception-free API: `offer` / `poll` / `peek` (vs `add`/`remove`/`element`)"},
		{"id":"qc2","type":"text","x":1500,"y":230,"width":640,"height":130,"text":"## PriorityQueue\n- Binary **min-heap**; `offer`/`poll` O(log n), `peek` O(1)\n- Iteration order is NOT sorted — only `poll` order is\n- Custom order via `Comparator`"},
		{"id":"map","type":"file","file":"03 Java/05 Collections Framework/12 Map.md","x":1500,"y":470,"width":250,"height":55,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"hashmap","type":"file","file":"03 Java/05 Collections Framework/13 HashMap.md","x":1500,"y":550,"width":250,"height":55},
		{"id":"linkedhashmap","type":"file","file":"03 Java/05 Collections Framework/14 LinkedHashMap.md","x":1500,"y":625,"width":250,"height":55},
		{"id":"treemap","type":"file","file":"03 Java/05 Collections Framework/15 TreeMap.md","x":1500,"y":700,"width":250,"height":55},
		{"id":"hashtable","type":"file","file":"03 Java/05 Collections Framework/16 Hashtable.md","x":1500,"y":775,"width":250,"height":55},
		{"id":"concurrenthashmap","type":"file","file":"03 Java/05 Collections Framework/17 ConcurrentHashMap.md","x":1500,"y":850,"width":250,"height":55},
		{"id":"hashc","type":"text","x":1790,"y":545,"width":460,"height":420,"text":"## HashMap internals\n- index = `(n-1) & spread(hash)`, `spread = h ^ (h>>>16)`\n- Default capacity **16**, **load factor 0.75** → resize (double) at 12 entries\n- Collision → linked list; **treeify at 8 nodes when cap ≥ 64** → Red-Black Tree O(log n); untreeify at 6\n- One `null` key, many `null` values\n\n### Variants\n- **LinkedHashMap**: insertion/access order → **LRU cache** (`removeEldestEntry`)\n- **TreeMap**: red-black tree, sorted keys, O(log n), `NavigableMap`\n- **Hashtable**: legacy, whole-map `synchronized`, no nulls"},
		{"id":"iterator","type":"file","file":"03 Java/05 Collections Framework/02 Iterator.md","x":-20,"y":860,"width":250,"height":55,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"eqhc","type":"text","x":-20,"y":935,"width":560,"height":100,"text":"## equals() & hashCode()\nEqual ⇒ equal hashCode. Use same fields via `Objects.hash`.\nMutating key fields after insertion → entry becomes unreachable."},
		{"id":"cmp","type":"text","x":-20,"y":1045,"width":560,"height":100,"text":"## Comparable vs Comparator\n`Comparable` = natural order (`compareTo`). `Comparator` = external/composable (`comparing().thenComparing()`). Never `a - b` (overflow)."},
		{"id":"failfast","type":"text","x":-20,"y":1155,"width":560,"height":110,"text":"## Fail-fast vs Fail-safe iterators\nFail-fast: `modCount` mismatch → `ConcurrentModificationException` (ArrayList/HashMap). Fail-safe: iterate a snapshot (CopyOnWrite, CHM). Remove via `Iterator.remove` / `removeIf`."},
		{"id":"streams","type":"text","x":-20,"y":1275,"width":560,"height":95,"text":"## Streams integration\n`collection.stream()…collect(...)` — lazy, single-use.\n`Collectors.toMap / groupingBy / partitioningBy / joining`."},
		{"id":"concurrent","type":"file","file":"03 Java/05 Collections Framework/18 Concurrent Collections.md","x":2380,"y":470,"width":250,"height":55,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"chmc","type":"text","x":2380,"y":550,"width":560,"height":120,"text":"## ConcurrentHashMap\nLock-free reads; per-bin CAS / `synchronized` on writes (no segments, Java 8+). Weakly-consistent iterators; no nulls. Use `computeIfAbsent` / `merge` for atomic updates."},
		{"id":"cowc","type":"text","x":2380,"y":685,"width":560,"height":90,"text":"## CopyOnWriteArrayList / Set\nEvery write copies the array → read-mostly workloads (listeners, config)."},
		{"id":"bqc","type":"text","x":2380,"y":790,"width":560,"height":100,"text":"## BlockingQueue\n`ArrayBlockingQueue` / `LinkedBlockingQueue` — `put`/`take` block → producer/consumer handoff."},
		{"id":"skiplistc","type":"text","x":2380,"y":905,"width":560,"height":90,"text":"## ConcurrentSkipListMap / Set\nSorted **and** concurrent, O(log n) — the concurrent TreeMap."},
		{"id":"syncc","type":"text","x":2380,"y":1010,"width":560,"height":90,"text":"## synchronizedXxx wrappers\n`Collections.synchronizedMap/List` lock the whole object; still need manual sync to iterate. Prefer j.u.c."}
	],
